;
; Test-only stimulus: replays a precomputed single-ended RXD waveform to drive the
; RX decoder on-chip, one bit per 50 ns half-bit (6 cycles at 120 MHz, matching
; the RX SM's half-bit). Half-bit levels are pulled LSB-first from the FIFO and
; driven onto the RXD injection pin; a companion GPIO holds RXC (carrier) so the
; decoder is gated exactly as on the wire.

.program rx_stimulus

.wrap_target
    out pins, 1 [5]
.wrap
